        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9a653a81-733f-5c92-9981-db7e2d2a3ba2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Songs: \"Mmm Papi\", \"La Isla Bonita\", \"Whiplash\", \"Rock Me In\"\n- People: Madonna, Patrick Leonard, Bruce Gaitsch, Selena Gomez & the Scene\n- Albums: \"True Blue\"\n- Places: San Pedro Town\n\nFacts:\n- In 1984, San Pedro Town was granted town status, and it was sometimes said to have inspired Madonna's song \"La Isla Bonita,\" which opens with the line \"last night I dreamt of San Pedro.\"\n- In 1986, Madonna released \"La Isla Bonita\" on her third studio album \"True Blue.\"\n- Madonna and Patrick Leonard co-wrote and co-produced \"La Isla Bonita,\" and Bruce Gaitsch contributed additional songwriting.\n- In 1987, \"La Isla Bonita\" was noted as a Latin pop song.\n- The same writers together wrote \"Mmm Papi,\" \"Rock Me In,\" and \"Whiplash.\"\n- \"Mmm Papi\" was noted for having a Latin pop influence similar to Madonna's \"La Isla Bonita.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d735a6d6-2b44-5499-ab4a-e31a623222bb",
        "text": "Page: Mmm Papi. Sentence: \"Mmm Papi\" is noted for having a Latin pop influence, similar to Madonna's \"La Isla Bonita\" (1987).\nPage: La Isla Bonita. Sentence: \"La Isla Bonita\" (English: The Beautiful Island ) is a song by American singer Madonna from her third studio album \"True Blue\" (1986).\nPage: La Isla Bonita. Sentence: She and Patrick Leonard co-wrote and co-produced the song, and Bruce Gaitsch provided additional songwriting.\nPage: Whiplash (Selena Gomez &amp; the Scene song). Sentence: Together, they wrote \"Mmm Papi\", \"Rock Me In\" and \"Whiplash\".\nPage: San Pedro Town. Sentence: The once sleepy fishing village was granted the status of a town in 1984 and was sometimes said to be the inspiration for the song \"La Isla Bonita\" (which begins with the line \"last night I dreamt of San Pedro\"), written by Madonna, Patrick Leonard and Bruce Gaitsch.",
